Source of motanka-stack-shell: Quickshell 0.3.2, the desktop shell of
upstream Omarchy v4.5.0, and cpptrace 1.0.4 (shared, with libunwind and a
bundled libdwarf-lite), under /opt/motanka, for both suites.

The upstream tarballs are listed in stack/shell-components.tsv (imported by
build-imports); test/vm/build fetches them with stack/fetch-sources
--components stack/shell-components.tsv.

Both suites build against motanka-qt6-dev (Qt 6.12 in /opt/motanka) and
the package depends on motanka-qt6: Upstream's shell needs Qt 6.11 or
later, and both archives carry 6.10 (design.md, "Qt for both releases").
motanka-qt6 and motanka-qt6-dev are locally built .debs, given to sbuild
with --extra-package (sbuild-local), so packaging/motanka-qt6 must be built
for the suite first. The build stops if the archive's Qt development files
are in the chroot, and the packaged quickshell must resolve every Qt
library from /opt/motanka/lib.
  noble     also gets motanka-stack-libs (GCC 16's C++ runtime, which
            motanka-qt6 depends on there), so packaging/motanka-stack is
            built first too. GCC 16 comes from the toolchain PPA
            (sbuild-repos).
  resolute  the archive's GCC 16 and C++ runtime.

Quickshell uses Qt's private API, so the package depends on exactly the
motanka-qt6 version it was built against (debian/shell-build.sh shlibs).
